Avalanche Kernel source and avalanche.elf are under ../LICENSE (MIT).
avalanche.iso additionally contains unmodified GNU GRUB 2.12-9+deb13u2
binaries from Debian, distributed under their respective licenses in
GRUB-COPYRIGHT. Corresponding upstream source and Debian patches/build
rules are included in grub-source/. GRUB is a separate bootloader, not
part of the Avalanche kernel. The kernel MIT license does not relicense GRUB.

This is an early x86 32-bit kernel, not a Linux-compatible distribution.
The ISO includes BIOS and x86-64 UEFI bootloaders; Secure Boot signatures
are not provided. Console input supports PS/2 and COM1 serial, not native
USB. Files are volatile RAM files. There is no userspace, scheduler,
persistent disk filesystem, network stack, or package manager.
Images were compiled but have not been boot-tested.
